# FinanceTracker Application Structure and Features

This document summarizes the application structure and features as described in the README file for the FinanceTracker Flutter app.

## Overview
FinanceTracker is an Android-first Flutter app to track personal expenses, investments, and provide dashboards, charts, and backup options. It supports manual entry and automatic SMS parsing for bank/card messages (Android only).

### Key Features
- Manual expense & investment entry
- SMS parsing to auto-add transactions (Android)
- Local offline storage using SQLite (`finance.db`)
- Local JSON backups (auto daily + manual)
- Manual Google Drive backup & restore
- Export to CSV (optional)
- PIN/biometric lock (optional)

## Project Structure
```
lib/
  main.dart
  models/
    expense.dart
    investment.dart
  services/
    db_service.dart
    sms_service.dart
    backup_service.dart
  providers/
    expense_provider.dart
    investment_provider.dart
  screens/
    home_screen.dart
    add_expense_screen.dart
    add_investment_screen.dart
    backups_screen.dart
```

## Folder and File Descriptions
- **models/**: Data models for expenses and investments
- **services/**: Business logic for database, SMS parsing, and backup/restore
- **providers/**: State management for expenses and investments
- **screens/**: UI screens for home, adding expenses/investments, and backups
- **main.dart**: App entry point, theming, routing, and provider setup

## Implementation Notes
- Uses `provider` for state management
- SQLite for local storage (to be implemented)
- SMS parsing for Android (to be implemented)
- Backup/restore logic (to be implemented)
- UI navigation between main features (to be implemented)

---
This document serves as a reference for the initial setup and feature plan for the FinanceTracker app.